research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-107-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-108-The Statement allows `K = ∅`, but current Fact `[L3]` gives only a nonempty finite-list formulation and then appends that the empty set is compact. The cited Definition in `def-open-cover-r` says instead: “for every open cover U of K, either K = ∅ and the empty subfamily covers it, or there are n in N and U_0,...,U_n in U” covering K. With `K = ∅` and an empty cover family, current step 3.1 cannot obtain `W_0,...,W_n`.
