research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-43-{"id":"cor-boundedness-theorem-r","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Compact_space"],"rationale":"The Encyclopedia of Mathematics states that every real-valued continuous function on a compact space is bounded. The local corollary derives this immediately from compact image and Heine-Borel.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-44-{"id":"thm-extreme-value-r","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Compact_space"],"rationale":"The source states that a continuous real-valued function on compact space attains its largest and smallest values. The local theorem makes nonemptiness explicit and proves attainment from compactness of the image.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-45-{"id":"thm-intermediate-value","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/04%3A_Function_Limits_and_Continuity/4.09%3A_The_Intermediate_Value_Property"],"rationale":"Zakon states the intermediate value theorem for a continuous real function on an interval. The local proof adapts the standard bisection argument with a canonical left-half rule.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-46-{"id":"cor-continuous-image-of-an-interval-is-an-interval","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/04%3A_Function_Limits_and_Continuity/4.09%3A_The_Intermediate_Value_Property"],"rationale":"The source identifies the Darboux property with interval images. The local corollary derives order-convexity from IVT and adds the closed-bounded-image conclusion via compactness.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-47-{"id":"thm-one-dimensional-fixed-point","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://kconrad.math.uconn.edu/blurbs/analysis/contraction.pdf"],"rationale":"Conrad’s introduction states exactly that every continuous self-map of an arbitrary closed interval has a fixed point and proves it by applying IVT to f(x)-x. The local proof is that argument in the reversed sign convention.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-48-{"id":"lem-monotone-with-interval-image-is-continuous","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/04%3A_Function_Limits_and_Continuity/4.09%3A_The_Intermediate_Value_Property"],"rationale":"Zakon proves that a monotone function with the Darboux property on an interval is continuous, including relative endpoint continuity. The local hypothesis that the image is order-convex is exactly the Darboux property for a monotone map.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
