research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-50-{"id":"lem-real-and-metric-notions-agree","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Introduction_to_Real_Analysis_%28Trench%29/08%3A_Metric_Spaces/8.00%3A_Introduction_to_Metric_Spaces","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_unifcont.html"],"rationale":"The sources give the metric versions of continuity, uniform continuity, Lipschitz conditions, and compactness on real subspaces. The local item is a direct dictionary across already defined notions, with convention details written out.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-51-{"id":"thm-heine-cantor-r","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Introduction_to_Real_Analysis_%28Trench%29/08%3A_Metric_Spaces/8.00%3A_Introduction_to_Metric_Spaces","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_unifcont.html"],"rationale":"The sources state that a continuous function on a compact set is uniformly continuous. The local proof adapts the standard sequential contradiction and explicitly accounts for its countable selection.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-52-{"id":"cor-continuous-extension-from-a-dense-subset-r","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/Practice-Final-3.18.100.pdf"],"rationale":"The MIT problem states the unique extension of a uniformly continuous map from a dense subset into a complete target. The local corollary specializes to real subspaces and records that the extension remains uniformly continuous.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-53-{"id":"thm-holder-exponent-above-one-forces-constancy","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.cs.cornell.edu/~bindel/nmds/00-Background/04-Calculus.html"],"rationale":"Cornell’s notes state exactly that the only alpha-Hölder functions for alpha greater than one are constant. The local proof expands the standard equal-partition estimate for rational exponents.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-54-{"id":"thm-compactness-is-necessary-for-evt-and-uniform-continuity","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.lehman.edu/faculty/rbettiol/lehman_teaching/2020mat320/baby_Rudin.pdf"],"rationale":"Rudin Theorem 4.20 states exactly the three clauses: on noncompact E there are an unbounded continuous function and a bounded continuous function with no maximum, and bounded noncompact E supports a non-uniformly-continuous continuous function. The local proof follows that theorem.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
